,"references":[],"explanation74":"Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum in New York belongs to Organic architecture. Its defining role is museum with a continuous spiral ramp.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0366","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0366","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Villa Barbaro?","value":"Renaissance","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Villa Barbaro in Maser belongs to Renaissance. Its defining role is villa integrating residence and agricultural wings.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0367","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0367","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Laurentian Library vestibule?","value":"Mannerist","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Laurentian Library vestibule in Florence belongs to Mannerist. Its defining role is library entrance with a monumental stair.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0368","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0368","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Reims Cathedral?","value":"Gothic","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Reims Cathedral in Reims belongs to Gothic. Its defining role is french coronation cathedral.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0369","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0369","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which part of San Carlo alle Quattro Fontane faces the street with alternating concave and convex bays?","value":"Façade","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Borromini gave the street façade a strongly undulating composition.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0370","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0370","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Glass Pavilion?","value":"Expressionism","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Glass Pavilion in Cologne belongs to Expressionism. Its defining role is exhibition pavilion for the glass industry.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0371","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0371","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Palazzo Rucellai?","value":"Renaissance","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Palazzo Rucellai in Florence belongs to Renaissance. Its defining role is urban palace with superposed pilasters.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0372","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0372","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Santa Maria Novella façade?","value":"Renaissance","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Santa Maria Novella façade in Florence belongs to Renaissance. Its defining role is church façade integrating medieval fabric.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0373","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0373","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Walden 7?","value":"Postmodernism","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Walden 7 in Sant Just Desvern belongs to Postmodernism. Its defining role is housing grouped around multiple courtyards.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0374","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0374","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Altes Museum?","value":"Neoclassical","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Altes Museum in Berlin belongs to Neoclassical. Its defining role is public museum.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0375","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0375","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Jewish Museum Berlin?","value":"Deconstructivist","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Jewish Museum Berlin in Berlin belongs to Deconstructivist. Its defining role is museum with voids and fractured axes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0376","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0376","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Teatro Olimpico?","value":"Renaissance","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Teatro Olimpico in Vicenza belongs to Renaissance. Its defining role is permanent indoor theatre.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0377","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0377","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Casa Batlló?","value":"Catalan Modernisme","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Casa Batlló in Barcelona belongs to Catalan Modernisme. Its defining role is remodelled urban house.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0378","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0378","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Würzburg Residence?","value":"Baroque","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Würzburg Residence in Würzburg belongs to Baroque. Its defining role is prince-bishop's residence.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0379","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0379","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which feature differentiates the cloister of San Carlo alle Quattro Fontane from a simple rectangular arcade?","value":"Convex corner bays","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Borromini articulated the small cloister with unusual corner treatments and curved elements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0380","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0380","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Palazzo Carignano?","value":"Baroque","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Palazzo Carignano in Turin belongs to Baroque. Its defining role is palace with a curved brick façade.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0381","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0381","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Villa Farnese at Caprarola?","value":"Mannerist","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Villa Farnese at Caprarola in Caprarola belongs to Mannerist. Its defining role is pentagonal palace with circular court.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0382","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0382","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Santo Spirito?","value":"Renaissance","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Santo Spirito in Florence belongs to Renaissance. Its defining role is basilican church.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0383","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0383","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with San Sebastiano?","value":"Renaissance","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"San Sebastiano in Mantua belongs to Renaissance. Its defining role is central-plan church.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0384","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0384","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with La Scala?","value":"Neoclassical","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"La Scala in Milan belongs to Neoclassical. Its defining role is opera house.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0385","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0385","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Temple of Concordia?","value":"Doric","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Temple of Concordia in Agrigento belongs to Doric. Its defining role is greek temple later used as a church.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0386","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0386","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Arab World Institute?","value":"High-tech","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Arab World Institute in Paris belongs to High-tech. Its defining role is cultural institute with patterned light-control devices.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0387","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0387","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Royal Palace of Caserta?","value":"Baroque","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Royal Palace of Caserta in Caserta belongs to Baroque. Its defining role is bourbon royal residence.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0388","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0388","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Modena Cathedral?","value":"Romanesque","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Modena Cathedral in Modena belongs to Romanesque. Its defining role is cathedral.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0389","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0389","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Horta’s Hôtel Tassel integrates an open stair hall with daylight entering principally from:","value":"A roof light","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The central stair hall is lit from above, helping unite the interior across levels.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0390","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0390","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Yale Art and Architecture Building?","value":"Brutalism","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Yale Art and Architecture Building in New Haven belongs to Brutalism. Its defining role is university building with textured concrete.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0391","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0391","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with San Miniato al Monte?","value":"Romanesque","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"San Miniato al Monte in Florence belongs to Romanesque. Its defining role is basilica.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0392","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0392","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Milan Cathedral?","value":"Gothic","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Milan Cathedral in Milan belongs to Gothic. Its defining role is cathedral in candoglia marble.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0393","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0393","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Glyptothek?","value":"Neoclassical","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Glyptothek in Munich belongs to Neoclassical. Its defining role is sculpture museum.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0394","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0394","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Terragni’s Casa del Fascio in Como organises its spaces around a:","value":"Central covered hall","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its compact block is organised around a central assembly space, linking circulation and public functions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0395","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0395","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Vierzehnheiligen?","value":"Baroque","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Vierzehnheiligen in Bad Staffelstein belongs to Baroque. Its defining role is pilgrimage church.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0396","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0396","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Schröder House?","value":"De Stijl","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Schröder House in Utrecht belongs to De Stijl. Its defining role is house with transformable upper-floor partitions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0397","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0397","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"A tetrastyle temple front has how many columns?","value":"Four","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Tetrastyle denotes a front with four columns; hexastyle has six and octastyle eight.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0398","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0398","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Vitra Fire Station?","value":"Deconstructivist","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Vitra Fire Station in Weil am Rhein belongs to Deconstructivist. Its defining role is fire station later used for exhibitions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0399","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0399","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Nakagin Capsule Tower?","value":"Metabolism","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Nakagin Capsule Tower in Tokyo belongs to Metabolism. Its defining role is tower of prefabricated capsules.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0400","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0400","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Villa Farnesina?","value":"Renaissance","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Villa Farnesina in Rome belongs to Renaissance. Its defining role is suburban villa for agostino chigi.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0401","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0401","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with San Vitale?","value":"Byzantine","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"San Vitale in Ravenna belongs to Byzantine. Its defining role is central-plan church.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0402","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0402","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Il Redentore?","value":"Renaissance","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Il Redentore in Venice belongs to Renaissance. Its defining role is votive church.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0403","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0403","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Panthéon?","value":"Neoclassical","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Panthéon in Paris belongs to Neoclassical. Its defining role is church converted into a national mausoleum.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0404","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0404","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with La Muralla Roja?","value":"Postmodernism","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"La Muralla Roja in Calpe belongs to Postmodernism. Its defining role is housing complex of coloured interlocking stairs.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0405","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0405","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Guggenheim Museum Bilbao?","value":"Deconstructivist","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Guggenheim Museum Bilbao in Bilbao belongs to Deconstructivist. Its defining role is art museum with titanium cladding.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0406","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0406","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with HSBC headquarters?","value":"High-tech","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"HSBC headquarters in Hong Kong belongs to High-tech. Its defining role is bank headquarters with suspended floors.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0407","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0407","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with San Giorgio Maggiore?","value":"Renaissance","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"San Giorgio Maggiore in Venice belongs to Renaissance. Its defining role is monastic church with temple-front façade.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0408","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0408","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Rockefeller Center?","value":"Art Deco","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Rockefeller Center in New York belongs to Art Deco. Its defining role is commercial and cultural complex.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0409","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0409","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural tradition is most closely associated with Chartres Cathedral?","value":"Gothic","group":"Architectural styles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Chartres Cathedral in Chartres belongs to Gothic. Its defining role is cathedral with extensive stained glass.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0410","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0410","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a thermal bridge in a building envelope?","value":"A path of increased heat transfer","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"A thermal bridge conducts heat more readily than surrounding parts of the envelope, often at junctions or structural elements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0411","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0411","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"At Hagia Sophia, what connects the main dome to the square arrangement of its four principal supports?","value":"Pendentives","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Curved triangular pendentives mediate between the circular dome and its supporting square.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0412","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0412","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The unusually shallow choir at Santa Maria presso San Satiro is resolved through:","value":"Perspective relief","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Bramante created the impression of a deep choir within a very restricted physical depth.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0413","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0413","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Murazzi on the Venetian littoral were constructed primarily as:","value":"Sea defences","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Murazzi are major masonry sea defences protecting parts of the Venetian lagoon's coastal barrier.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0414","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0414","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The church of Sant’Andrea in Mantua was built partly to accommodate pilgrims venerating a relic of:","value":"The blood of Christ","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The church is associated with the relic of the Precious Blood, which helped shape its pilgrimage role.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0415","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0415","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which relationship is characteristic of the Laurentian Library vestibule's wall treatment?","value":"Columns appear recessed into the wall","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Michelangelo placed paired columns within wall recesses, challenging conventional classical articulation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0416","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0416","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Teatro all'Antica at Sabbioneta was designed by:","value":"Vincenzo Scamozzi","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Scamozzi designed the Teatro all'Antica as a purpose-built theatre for Sabbioneta's ducal court.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0417","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0417","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What visual effect characterises the Hall of the Giants at Palazzo Te?","value":"The room dissolves into a painted catastrophe","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Giulio Romano's painted architecture and collapsing figures envelop the visitor in an illusionistic scene.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0418","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0418","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Sant’Ivo alla Sapienza was designed to serve which institutional setting?","value":"A university","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The church stands within the historic Sapienza university complex in Rome.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0419","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0419","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which plan describes the main body of Bernini's Sant'Andrea al Quirinale?","value":"Transverse oval","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The long axis of the oval runs across, rather than along, the entrance-to-altar axis.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0420","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0420","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The principal space enclosed by Bernini's colonnades in Saint Peter's Square is approximately:","value":"Oval","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The sweeping colonnades enclose an approximately oval space, connected to the basilica by a trapezoidal forecourt.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0421","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0421","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"In an early Christian church, an ambo was used chiefly for:","value":"Reading scripture","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The ambo is a raised platform for liturgical readings, distinct from the altar, font and episcopal chair.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0422","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0422","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Westminster Hall's medieval timber roof is a celebrated example of a:","value":"Hammer-beam roof","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its hammer-beam construction spans the hall without a forest of supporting columns.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0423","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0423","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The central block and radiating wings at Stupinigi were designed around which court activity?","value":"Hunting","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Juvarra organised a Savoy hunting lodge around a central ceremonial salon.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0424","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0424","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The engineering experience behind Paxton's Crystal Palace was particularly connected with:","value":"Large greenhouses","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Paxton transferred techniques of modular iron-and-glass greenhouse construction to an exhibition building.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0425","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0425","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architect designed Habitat 67 in Montreal?","value":"Moshe Safdie","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Safdie developed Habitat 67 as an arrangement of prefabricated concrete housing modules for Expo 67.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0426","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0426","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II combines shopping with which nineteenth-century spatial type?","value":"Covered urban arcade","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its glazed roof turns intersecting pedestrian routes into a sheltered commercial interior.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0427","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0427","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"In Horta's Hôtel Tassel, ironwork and floor decoration are linked by:","value":"Flowing plant-like curves","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The interior exemplifies Art Nouveau's integration of structure, ornament and spatial design.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0428","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0428","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The roofscape of Casa Milà is especially known for sculptural:","value":"Chimneys and ventilation towers","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Gaudí treated rooftop services as an expressive architectural landscape.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0429","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0429","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The small metal discs visible on the Austrian Postal Savings Bank façade express the fixing of:","value":"Stone facing slabs","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Wagner made the fastening of facing panels part of the façade's visual language.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0430","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0430","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What does the glazed workshop wing at the Dessau Bauhaus chiefly reveal?","value":"Separation of façade and structural frame","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The curtain wall wraps the structural frame, making the workshops appear unusually open.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0431","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0431","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The upper floor of the Schröder House can be reorganised through:","value":"Sliding and folding partitions","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its movable partitions allow the living space to shift between open and subdivided arrangements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0432","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0432","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which feature occupies much of the upper level of Villa Savoye beside its enclosed rooms?","value":"A roof garden","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The roof garden is part of Le Corbusier's programme at Villa Savoye and one of his Five Points.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0433","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0433","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Barcelona Pavilion's walls chiefly demonstrate which idea?","value":"Space shaped by independent planes","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its freestanding wall planes articulate space without forming a conventional cellular load-bearing plan.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0434","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0434","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which department-store owner commissioned Fallingwater?","value":"Edgar Kaufmann","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Edgar and Liliane Kaufmann commissioned Wright's Fallingwater as a weekend retreat.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0435","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0435","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The broad horizontal roofs and low proportions of the Robie House are intended to emphasise:","value":"Continuity with the prairie landscape","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Wright's Prairie architecture stresses horizontality and the extension of interior space into the site.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0436","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0436","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"In the Marseille Unité d'Habitation, internal streets principally provide access to:","value":"Interlocking apartments","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The internal corridors serve apartments arranged within a large collective-housing structure.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0437","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0437","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which building combines a convent programme with individual cells and communal religious spaces?","value":"Sainte-Marie de La Tourette","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Le Corbusier's La Tourette was designed for a Dominican community.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0438","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0438","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The court at the Salk Institute is visually directed toward the ocean by a narrow:","value":"Water channel","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The linear water feature reinforces the axis through the open court toward the Pacific.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0439","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0439","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Daylight in the Kimbell Art Museum's original galleries is controlled chiefly through:","value":"Roof slots and curved reflectors","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Kahn used roof openings and reflectors to diffuse daylight beneath the vaulted gallery roofs.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0440","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0440","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Seagram Building's setback from Park Avenue creates a:","value":"Public forecourt","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The plaza gives the tower an urban setting and a clear relationship to the street.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0441","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0441","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"At the Sendai Mediatheque, the irregular vertical tubes combine circulation and services with:","value":"Structural support","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Toyo Ito’s tubes carry loads and accommodate services or movement through the open floor plates.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0442","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0442","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The shell segments of the Sydney Opera House were ultimately developed from the geometry of a:","value":"Sphere","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"A common spherical geometry made the different roof segments more consistent for construction.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0443","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0443","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The widened upper portion of Torre Velasca is often read as a reference to:","value":"Historic Lombard towers","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"BBPR's modern tower evokes aspects of Milan's historic architectural skyline without copying it literally.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0444","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0444","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Carlo Scarpa is buried within which complex of his own design?","value":"Brion Memorial","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Scarpa was buried at the Brion complex near San Vito d'Altivole, which he had designed.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0445","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0445","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The bright service elements on the Centre Pompidou's exterior support which design strategy?","value":"Freeing large internal floors","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Placing services and circulation externally helped create large adaptable interior spaces.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0446","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0446","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The accessible ramps in the reconstructed Reichstag dome allow visitors to move above the:","value":"Parliamentary chamber","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Foster’s dome gives the public an elevated relationship to the parliamentary space below.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0447","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0447","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The thermal baths at Vals make extensive visual use of locally associated:","value":"Quartzite slabs","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Zumthor's stacked stone surfaces connect the bathing spaces to the Alpine geology.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0448","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0448","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Kolumba in Cologne preserves a connection with the city's past by incorporating:","value":"The ruins of a church","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Zumthor's museum integrates the surviving ruins of Saint Kolumba and an existing chapel.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0449","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0449","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Church of the Light is especially defined by a cruciform:","value":"Opening cut through a concrete wall","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Ando turns a cross-shaped wall opening into the interior's principal source of symbolic light.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0450","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0450","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Rolex Learning Center's continuous interior is characterised by:","value":"An undulating floor with open courtyards","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"SANAA used a gently varying floor surface and courtyards to organise a connected learning environment.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0451","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0451","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What distinguishes a stereobate from the stylobate in a Greek temple platform?","value":"It comprises the lower supporting steps","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The stylobate is the upper platform bearing the columns; the stereobate refers to the supporting stepped substructure below.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0452","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0452","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Montreal Biosphere demonstrates the structural principle of a:","value":"Geodesic dome","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its spherical lattice distributes forces through a network of interconnected elements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0453","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0453","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Vanna Venturi House deliberately challenges strict modernist restraint through its:","value":"Oversized gable and contradictory composition","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Venturi used familiar house elements in an intentionally complex and sometimes contradictory composition.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0454","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0454","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The Capitol Complex at Chandigarh groups the Assembly with the High Court and the:","value":"Secretariat","group":"Architecture and society","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Secretariat, High Court and Legislative Assembly form the principal governmental buildings of the Capitol Complex.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0455","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0455","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Place these events in chronological order, from earliest to latest.\nA. Italian armistice announced\nB. Apollo 11 Moon landing\nC. Gagarin's first human spaceflight","value":"A → C → B","group":"Historical sequence","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"Existing Tapestry historical record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Italian%20armistice%20announced","recordId":"t68-c77edd7fb09d","supportScope":"Saved chronological reference; not newly fetched"},{"file":"Existing Tapestry historical record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Apollo%2011%20Moon%20landing","recordId":"t68-801652e3c3d3","supportScope":"Saved chronological reference; not newly fetched"},{"file":"Existing Tapestry historical record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Gagarin%27s%20first%20human%20spaceflight","recordId":"t68-6833d0768625","supportScope":"Saved chronological reference; not newly fetched"}],"explanation74":"Italian armistice announced (1943 CE); Gagarin's first human spaceflight (1961 CE); Apollo 11 Moon landing (1969 CE).","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0456","nodeId":"FACT101-ARC